SUMMARY:THE CLOVERHEARTS (AUS) (Uhrzeit prüfen)
LOCATION:Chelsea
DESCRIPTION: The Story So Far... THE CLOVERHEARTS are one of the newest and fastest-growing bands in today’s Celtic punk scene. Fronted by Australian singer-songwriter Sam Cooper\, the band has racked up millions of streams online in just a few short years\, while performing alongside genre giants such as The Mahones\, Flogging Molly\, Ferocious Dog\, Zebrahead\, and Booze & Glory\, to name a few. Raised on a strict diet of skate punk and Jägerbombs\, Sam fuses upbeat\, angst-driven rock with whimsical tales of love and loss - resulting in roaring bagpipe anthems and twisted tin-whistle earworms reminiscent of early Dropkick Murphys meets Green Day. Cemented alongside scene stalwarts like The Real McKenzies and The Rumjacks on Spotify’s Official Celtic Punk Playlist\, the explosive growth of their music speaks for itself - resonating just as well with kickflippin’ street punks as with boozy Pogues fans. In their short five-year career\, The Cloverhearts have taken the stage at some of the biggest festivals in Europe\, the UK\, and Japan - including Punk Rock Holiday (SI)\, Brakrock (BE)\, Mighty Sounds (CZ)\, Rock im Ring (IT)\, Rebellion (UK)\, Brintaal (IT)\, and Festival du Roi Arthur (FR)\, among many others. As the band roars into 2026 with a new lineup and a new album on the horizon\, The Cloverhearts truly have the world at their fingertips - and they plan on taking it for keeps. www.thecloverhearts.com/ www.facebook.com/thecloverhearts Tickets: www.eventim-light.com/at/a/60fa5dffd95e696e2fb33355/e/6a00c291408fedea0a9262af
URL:https://www.chelsea.co.at/concerts.php#concert_6711
